# GaAs, zincblende, conventional (non-primitive) cubic cell: 4 Ga + 4 As,
# a = 5.6533 Ang (the real, textbook experimental GaAs lattice constant).
# The Ga sublattice is FCC -- geometrically frustrated for the pair-cluster
# enumeration stb-gqca does (see the README's Section 2: no 2-coloring of
# an FCC lattice makes every nearest-neighbor pair unlike, the same reason
# rocksalt's own cation sublattice can't reach it either). This is real,
# unavoidable physics of the zincblende structure, not a fixture quirk --
# the walkthrough shows exactly how stb-gqca reports and works around it.
# --sublattice Ga --species-b Al models Al(x)Ga(1-x)As; --species-b <X>
# models any other III-V pseudobinary built on the same GaAs host lattice.
SystemName GaAs zincblende (conventional cubic cell)
SystemLabel siesta

LatticeConstant 5.6533 Ang
%block LatticeVectors
  1.0000000000   0.0000000000   0.0000000000
  0.0000000000   1.0000000000   0.0000000000
  0.0000000000   0.0000000000   1.0000000000
%endblock LatticeVectors

NumberOfSpecies 2
%block ChemicalSpeciesLabel
 1  31  Ga
 2  33  As
%endblock ChemicalSpeciesLabel

NumberOfAtoms 8
AtomicCoordinatesFormat Fractional
%block AtomicCoordinatesAndAtomicSpecies
 0.00 0.00 0.00  1
 0.00 0.50 0.50  1
 0.50 0.00 0.50  1
 0.50 0.50 0.00  1
 0.25 0.25 0.25  2
 0.25 0.75 0.75  2
 0.75 0.25 0.75  2
 0.75 0.75 0.25  2
%endblock AtomicCoordinatesAndAtomicSpecies
